---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';const d='/equipment/03-07/',photo='https://indico.cern.ch/event/176828/contributions/1442743/attachments/230195/322092/prezentacja_Aachen.pdf#page=3',drawing='https://www.nanofab.utah.edu/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/Oxford-80-Manual.pdf';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Oxford Plasmalab 80 Plus visual station" description="Inspect a metric enclosure and evaluate a hypothetical dry witness fixture without operating a process." wide={true}><article id="oxford" class="equipment"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/03-07/">← Equipment 03-07</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#ox-evidence">Evidence</a></nav><header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">03-07 / NON-OPERATIONAL INSPECTION</p><h2>Does the dry witness fit?</h2><p class="eq-lede">Open the model’s schematic cutaway and compare a circular dummy with a 120 mm reference boundary. A centered 100 mm dummy leaves 10 mm radial clearance. The original process is not simulated.</p></header>
<div class="o-cols"><section><h3>Oxford Plasmalab 80 Plus</h3><canvas id="ox-model" aria-label="Orbitable Oxford 80 Plus enclosure and illustrative dry stage cutaway"></canvas><p id="ox-viewstatus" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><button id="ox-station">Whole unit / reset view</button><button id="ox-stage">Stage close-up</button><button id="ox-rear">Rear view</button><p>Click the blue hood to see the schematic cutaway, or the marked reference plate to check dry fit. No actual equipment operation is represented.</p></section>
<section><h3>Dry geometry only</h3><label>Dummy disc diameter<select id="ox-size"><option value="100">100 mm</option><option value="60">60 mm</option><option value="140">140 mm</option></select></label><div class="o-fields"><label>X offset, mm<input id="ox-x" type="number" min="-30" max="30" step="any" value="0"/></label><label>Z offset, mm<input id="ox-z" type="number" min="-30" max="30" step="any" value="0"/></label></div><label>Fictional map<select id="ox-map"><option value="thin">Static reference I</option><option value="thick">Static reference II</option></select></label><button id="ox-inspect">Open schematic cutaway</button><button id="ox-check">Check dry fit</button><button id="ox-reset">Restore view</button><p id="ox-status" role="status"></p></section></div>
<section><h3>Read-only result</h3><div class="o-cols"><div><p id="ox-read" role="status"></p><button id="ox-export">Download static inspection JSON</button><p><a href={d+'example-static-report.json'}>Example</a>. The signed clearance is 60 mm minus the dummy radius and center displacement. A zero clearance is exact tangency in this ideal fixture; negative means outside. Dummy shape and thickness map are independent, not a recipe or material result.</p></div><canvas id="ox-mapcanvas" width="440" height="220" aria-label="Immutable fictional thickness reference matrix"/></div></section>
<section id="ox-evidence"><h3>Visual references and checks</h3><p>Oxford Plasmalab 80 Plus PECVD enclosure: steel cabinet, blue chamber hood, front control shapes and adjacent terminal, based on the <a href={photo}>institutional installation photograph, slide 3</a>. <a href={drawing}>Oxford installation data, issue 6, diagrams 2-1 and 2-2</a> give a typical 580 × 790 mm footprint and 1430 mm height for the selected cabinet/chamber variant. Controls are decorative; console position, stage radius, fittings and cutaway travel are authored estimates. No process-service routing is modeled.</p><div class="o-cols"><figure><img alt="Original Oxford 80 Plus exterior rendering" src={d+'station.webp'}/><figcaption>Original cabinet and hood geometry. Compare the linked installation photograph.</figcaption></figure><figure><img alt="Original dry dummy fit cutaway" src={d+'stage.webp'}/><figcaption>Original dry inspection cutaway, not mechanical travel or chamber operation.</figcaption></figure></div><table><thead><tr><th>Independent fixture check</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>100 mm centered circle</td><td>10 mm clearance</td><td>10 mm; fits</td></tr><tr><td>100 mm with (+6,+8) mm offset</td><td>Tangent at 0 mm</td><td>0 mm; fits</td></tr><tr><td>140 mm centered</td><td>−10 mm</td><td>−10 mm; does not fit</td></tr><tr><td>Pure capacitor algebra at two frozen map centers</td><td>C<sub>I</sub>/C<sub>II</sub>=2 at equal area/ε</td><td>800/400 = 2; no fringing or process model</td></tr></tbody></table><p><a href={d+'build-model.py'}>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={d+'oxford80plus.glb'}>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={d+'dry-fit.mjs'}>Dry fit and fixed data</a> · <a href={d+'vr.json'}>VR bounds and schematic pose</a>. No hardware or headset verification claimed.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/03-07/client.mjs';</script>
<style is:global>#oxford .o-cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.12fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem}#oxford section{padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);margin:1rem 0;min-width:0}#oxford :is(input,select,button){font:inherit;color:inherit;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.45rem;max-width:100%;box-sizing:border-box}#oxford .o-fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.4rem}#oxford label{display:grid;gap:.2rem;min-width:0;margin:.35rem 0}#oxford label :is(input,select){width:100%;min-width:0}#oxford button{margin:.35rem .25rem .2rem 0;cursor:pointer}#oxford button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #b28d5e}#oxford button:disabled{opacity:.5}#ox-model{display:block;width:100%;height:336px;touch-action:none}#ox-mapcanvas{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}#oxford figure{margin:.5rem 0}#oxford figure img{width:100%}#oxford table{font-size:.9rem;border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;text-align:left}#oxford td,#oxford th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding:.35rem}@media(max-width:780px){#oxford .o-cols{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}#ox-model{height:282px}}</style>
